<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for release builds (Developer ID or ad-hoc), signed with the hardened runtime (scripts/sign-and-notarize.sh).

  Intentionally empty:
  - Arbor is not sandboxed (DEC-004): a file manager needs to reach any folder the user opens, so
    there is no com.apple.security.app-sandbox, and with it none of the sandbox-only keys such as
    com.apple.security.network.client. Unsandboxed apps can mount SMB shares, browse Bonjour and
    run helper tools (/usr/bin/smbutil, bsdtar, mdutil) without any entitlement.
  - No hardened-runtime exceptions are needed: no JIT, no unsigned executable memory, no
    DYLD_* environment variables, no plug-ins from other teams, and no Apple Events to other apps.
  Privacy prompts (Desktop, Documents, Downloads, removable and network volumes, local network)
  come from the usage descriptions in Info.plist, not from entitlements.
  Add a key here only with a comment saying which feature needs it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
